WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.867
Build the habit of using the explain command.

00:00:02.867 --> 00:00:10.777
The exact plan format in Spark is different from the plan you may see in Postgres, but the purpose is similar.

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:14.517
We want evidence about what the engine plans to do.

00:00:14.517 --> 00:00:20.867
Look for scans, filters, joins, aggregations, sorting, and exchanges.

00:00:20.867 --> 00:00:28.952
In Spark, exchanges are especially interesting because they often indicate that data will be redistributed between

00:00:28.952 --> 00:00:33.117
workers. You do not need to understand every line of the plan.

00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:37.893
Start by asking where the expensive movement and large scans may occur.
